<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows $46.9 mln on Sept 16.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows $46.9 mln on Sept 16.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $46.9 million surplus on Sept 16 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON SEPTEMBER 16</p>
<p>Exports: $176.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $136.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $194.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $188.1 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $46.9 million</p>
<p>SEPTEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.372 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.706 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $1.500 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.206 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $40 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
